          dealing: 'Each player is dealt 11 cards (in some variants 13). The remaining cards form the stock pile. One card is turned up to start the discard pile.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: "Form all cards in your hand into valid melds and 'go out' (empty your hand). Lowest cumulative score across all rounds wins.",
          gameplay: "1. **Draw**: On your turn, draw one card from the stock or take the top card from the discard pile. 2. **Melding**: You can lay down melds as soon as you have them. In the first round, you usually need a minimum 'opening' count (e.g., 30 or 40 points in some variants). 3. **Laying Off**: You can add cards to your own or opponents' existing melds on the table. 4. **Discard**: End your turn by discarding one card to the discard pile.",
          keyRules: [
            'Juego (Set): 3+ cards of same rank (different suits).',
            'Escalera (Sequence): 3+ consecutive cards of same suit.',
            'Jokers and sometimes 2s act as wildcards.',
            'Sequence cannot consist solely of wildcards.',
            'Must draw before melding or laying off.',
            'Must end turn with a discard (unless going out).',
            "Can lay off on opponents' melds once you've opened.",
            'Going out ends the round; remaining cards count as penalties.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Keep your Jokers! They are your best chance to complete a long sequence. However, if you see an opponent has only 2 cards left, discard your Joker immediately to avoid the 50-point penalty. Prioritize forming sequences over setsâ€”they're harder for opponents to block.",
          intermediate: "Opening Strategy: Don't 'open' (lay down cards) as soon as you hit the minimum if you have cards that could be easily played off by others. Wait until you can lay down most of your hand at once. Watch the discard pileâ€”if the player to your left keeps taking your discards, stop feeding them cards they need.",
          advanced: "Discard Control: Pay attention to what the person to your left is picking up from the discard pile. If they pick up a 7 of Spades, they are likely building a 'Seven' set or a Spades sequenceâ€”do not feed them Spades! The 'Loba' play: Sometimes hold a complete meld in hand to surprise opponents, going out unexpectedly when they think they have time.",
          tips: [
            "Prioritize 'Escaleras' (Sequences) over 'Juegos' (Sets). Sequences are easier to extend and yield more opportunities to 'lay off' cards later.",
            "In Loba, the 2 is often a 'clean' cardâ€”use it naturally in sequences rather than as a wildcard unless desperate.",
            "Watch opponents' card counts. When someone is down to 2-3 cards, be very careful about what you discard.",
            'If you have multiple possible melds, lay down the one that gives you the most flexibility for laying off remaining cards.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
